{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>You shall not rule over him with rigor.</b> Work that serves no need, in order to afflict him — do not say to him, 'Warm this cup for me,' when he does not need it; 'Hoe under the vine until I come.' Now perhaps you will say: he cannot tell whether it is for a need or not, and I myself say to him that it is for a need — this matter is given over to his heart. Therefore it says, ״וְיָרֵאתָ״ (verse 25:17)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:27.682367671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}